# Sharded Markdown aggregates are local rendered views. Their `.d/`
# directories are the committed source of truth; tracking these files
# recreates the merge hot spots that sharding exists to remove.
#
# This list must hold one line per entry in `DOC_SHARD_PLANS`
# (code/packages/typescript/human-language-data/src/doc-shard-cli.ts). An
# untracked-but-unignored aggregate is not safe merely because it is currently
# absent: `git add -A` puts it straight back, and the hot spot returns with it.
/code/learning/human-languages/BACKLOG.md
/code/learning/human-languages/hindi/CHANGELOG.md
/code/packages/typescript/human-language-data/CHANGELOG.md
/code/programs/typescript/language-ladder/CHANGELOG.md
/code/packages/rust/lang-aot/CHANGELOG.md
/code/packages/rust/algol-iir-compiler/CHANGELOG.md
/code/specs/data/adj-facts-stdlib/CHANGELOG.md
# Script Ductus is deliberately absent: it is already ignored by its own
# `code/packages/typescript/script-ductus/.gitignore`. A line was briefly added
# here claiming it had "never been ignored" -- that came from grepping this
# file alone, which cannot see a nested .gitignore.

