# Claude Code — only ignore machine-specific files
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Rust coverage (`cargo tarpaulin --engine llvm`, i.e. `-C instrument-coverage`).
# An instrumented process whose environment was cleared has no LLVM_PROFILE_FILE
# to write to, so its profile runtime falls back to `default_*.profraw` in the
# working directory. The chief-of-staff approval adapters spawn exactly such
# children, so measuring their coverage leaves these behind in the crate dir.
*.profraw

# Elixir
_build/
deps/
.elixir_ls/
.mix/
.mix_test_failures
*.beam
*.app
compile.*
ebin/
erl_crash.dump

# `build-native.sh` emits here by default (dist-native-qt, dist-native-swiftui,
# and so on). These are build outputs -- an emitted project plus a compiled app
# -- and one of them is a bundled JDK. Left untracked and unignored, a careless
# `git add -A` commits hundreds of megabytes of it.
code/programs/mosaic/*/dist-native-*/

# The single-file view of `lessons.d/`, rebuilt on demand by
# `code/scripts/lessons.py render`. Deliberately NOT committed: a shared
# aggregate is precisely the file whose removal stopped every pair of
# concurrent PRs from conflicting. Edit the shard, never this.
/lessons.md
